-- title:
--   Homomorphisms GL₂(ℚᵣ)→ℤ are multiples of v∘det
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, and let $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$ denote the group of invertible $2\times 2$ matrices over $\mathbb{Q}_r$ (indexed by `Fin 2`). Let $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r) \to \mathbb{Z}$ be a group homomorphism into the integers written multiplicatively, and assume it is the $r$-adic valuation of the determinant in the following precise sense: for every $g$ and every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, one has $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if there is a unit $u \in \mathbb{Z}_r^\times$ with $\det g = u\, r^{\,n}$ in $\mathbb{Q}_r$, where $u$ and $r$ are viewed in $\mathbb{Q}_r$ through the algebra map $\mathbb{Z}_r \to \mathbb{Q}_r$ (note the exponent $n$ is an integer power taken in $\mathbb{Q}_r$). Let $\nu : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r) \to \mathbb{Z}$ be an arbitrary group homomorphism into the multiplicative integers. The conclusion is that there exists an integer $c$ such that $\nu(g) = \mathrm{vdet}(g)^c$ for all $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$; additively, $\nu = c \cdot \mathrm{vdet}$, so every such $\nu$ is an integer multiple of the valuation of the determinant.
--
--   The statement records that $\mathrm{Hom}(\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r), \mathbb{Z})$ is generated by the valuation of the determinant: the commutator subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of a field forces such a homomorphism to factor through $\det$, and on $\mathbb{Q}_r^\times$ any homomorphism to $\mathbb{Z}$ kills the units $\mathbb{Z}_r^\times$. It is used in the Cerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where homomorphisms of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$ attached to heights, degrees of kernels and isogenies of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules have to be identified with multiples of $v \circ \det$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_forall_apply_eq_zpow_of_monoidHom_generalLinearGroup_padic.lean

